WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.460
While there's plenty to love about Spider-Man:
Far From Home, no movie is perfect.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.240
For every great, powerful moment the film
delivers, there must also come a responsibility

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.040
to acknowledge where the film came up short.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.100
Spoilers ahead.

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.840
While Homecoming introduced the world to Zendaya's
MJ, Far From Home brings her and Tom Holland's

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.460
Peter Parker together romantically, and it's
a delight.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.259
The two young actors are able to capture the
awkward, budding romance between the two high

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.880
schoolers with natural chemistry.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.600
It's a sweet, engaging relationship that holds
down the film as Spider-Man battles illusions,

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.060
responsibilities, and his grief over Tony
Stark's death.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.900
This version of MJ's a bit more sarcastic
than previous Spider-Man love interests in

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.700
movies and animated shows, but the core of
the character shines through beautifully.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.280
Meanwhile, Holland is as great as ever, playing
a Peter distinct from both Tobey Maguire and

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.500
Andrew Garfield's conceptions of the character
while remaining as recognizably Spider-Man

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.000
as ever.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.580
While the underlying subtext of Far From Home
is pretty clearly about Peter learning that…

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.300
"With great power comes great responsibility."

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.120
...the actual way the film connects different
parts of Peter's life is a lot less focused.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.860
Peter wants to rely on Mysterio because Tony
Stark's death has put a lot of pressure on

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.660
him, but why?

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:09.150
The first film was about Peter learning to
be a friendly neighborhood Spider-Man and

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.810
turning down a spot with the Avengers, so
the immediate turnaround in the very next

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.360
solo sequel feels weird.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.520
Even with that, Peter's desire for a vacation
is pretty relatable it's not like he's letting

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:23.590
a robber run off with money, he's just pretty
understandably relieved that a seemingly magic-using

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:27.180
superhero from another earth is willing to
take down elemental super-demons.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:31.100
That's not exactly something that's in Spidey's
wheelhouse to begin with, so the idea that

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:33.960
he's somehow failing to live up to his potential
rings false.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.460
It's been a long time coming, but we finally
got to see classic Spidey villain Mysterio

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.140
on the big screen.

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.150
The illusionist who uses movie magic to trick
and manipulate Spider-Man has seemed like

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.540
a perfect fit for Spidey's cinematic adventures.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.600
Surprisingly, though, we've never gotten a
proper adaptation.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:52.560
A planned Spider-Man 4 by Sam Raimi was once
rumored to have Bruce Campbell attached to

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:56.409
play the bowl-headed supervillain in a quick
cameo, but Far From Home gives the character

00:01:56.409 --> 00:01:58.120
the screen time that he's always deserved.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.119
Even better, Jake Gyllenhaal is phenomenal
as the tricky supervillain, functioning as

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:05.909
a sort of director and project lead for a
group of talented ex-employees with a grudge

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:07.060
against Tony Stark.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:11.560
Anyone who saw Nightcrawler would know that
Gyllenhaal has the chops to play a truly unsettling

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.860
villain, and his casting as Mysterio is a
delight.

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.940
It's a great performance as a great villain.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:20.300
Considering how much of Homecoming is about
Peter essentially dealing with two opposing

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.220
father figures in Tony Stark and the Vulture,
it makes sense that he'd spend most of Far

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:26.510
From Home mourning the loss of his heroic
mentor.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.750
However, the film goes beyond Peter wanting
to live up to Iron Man's superheroism.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.300
By the time the credits roll, Peter Parker's
basically become Iron Lad.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:38.460
First, he gets bionic sunglasses that seem
to basically be able to do anything related

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:39.180
to technology.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.960
Then, he's given a ride from Tony's old pal
and sidekick in a private plane, where he

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:45.270
designs his new technologically-advanced super-suit.

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.870
Even the villains he's fought in the movies
to date all exist directly as a result of

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.260
Tony Stark's poor decisions.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:54.300
It's a pretty far cry from the dumpster-diving
boy from Queens that audiences briefly saw

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:55.880
in Captain America: Civil War.

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.420
"Oh, what do we have here?

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:58.260
Retro-tech, huh?

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.060
Thrift store?"

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.260
"Salvation Army?"

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:01.360
"The garbage actually."

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:02.400
"You're a dumpster diver?"

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.120
"Yeah, I was…"

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.000
And it's a huge jump from the constantly down-on-his-luck
and rent-hungry Peter Parker of the comics

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.040
and previous films.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:15.020
Peter wanting to live up to the flawed ideal
of Tony is a great concept in theory.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.420
Still, when most of his own storyline revolves
so completely around Iron Man's, it chips

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.260
away at Spider-Man as a viable character in
his own right.

00:03:22.820 --> 00:03:26.220
The Sam Raimi Spider-Man films are undeniably
a product of their times.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:30.600
At turns both deeply embarrassed about superhero
movies as a genre and deeply committed to

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.090
full-on weirdness, there's plenty to love
and and plenty to loathe about the early-2000s

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:35.980
superhero trilogy.

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:41.140
However, one aspect of the films that's unquestionably
a success is J.K. Simmons' casting as belligerent

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.160
newspaper editor J. Jonah Jameson.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:44.860
"Put an ad on the front page.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.930
Cash money for a picture of Spider-Man.

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:48.560
He doesn't want to be famous?

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.840
I'll make him infamous!"

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:55.860
Thankfully, Far From Home's mid-credits sequence
features Simmons reprising his role as the

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.860
Spider-Man-hating newsman.

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.300
Here's hoping he gets an even bigger role
in the next one.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.600
Homecoming had some incredible cameos and
performances.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.560
Michael Keaton dazzled with an incredible
villain performance.

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.880
Marissa Tomei made the most of her limited
screen time.

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.280
Chris Evans appearing as Captain America in
a series of taped PSAs was delightful.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:16.440
But Hannibal Buress' laconic Coach Wilson
nearly stole the show from everyone in only

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:17.380
a couple of scenes.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.940
Your gym teacher will be conducting the Captain
America fitness challenge."

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.360
"Thank you Captain.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.100
I'm pretty sure this guy is a war criminal
now, but whatever, I have to show these videos,

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:26.980
it's required by the state."

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.160
While it doesn't necessarily make a whole
lot of sense for a gym teacher to go on a

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:35.620
class trip to Europe instead, Martin Starr
reprises his role as Mr. Harrington and J.B.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.660
Smoove joins as a new teacher, Mr. Dell it's
hard not to feel like we were robbed of seeing

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.840
Buress in Far From Home.

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:43.140
All we can do is hope that he returns for
the sequel.

